    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the numbers that decide this case, and the outcome follows from them. The driver's GPS trace shows he did reach the pickup and hold position inside the geofence, but for 240 seconds only — from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 17:15:00 to the cancellation at 17:19:00. The minimum wait for a large-venue pickup such as Plaza Singapura is 300 seconds. That 60-second shortfall is decisive: under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. The rider's claim that the driver cancelled after only a few minutes is therefore supported, and the SGD 8.00 charged is refunded. The amount itself was correctly calculated — the greater of the SGD 4.00 large-venue zone fee and the SGD 8.00 RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee — so the fare line reconciles with the fee schedule and no billing-integrity defect exists (POL-NS-08(d)).\n\nThe driver's arguments are accepted so far as they go, but they do not change the result. His arrival was genuine — 25 fixes at 24 m from the pin, stationary throughout — so POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) is not engaged, no false-arrival referral is recorded against him, and his request that the ruling say so is granted. He is also right that the rider's device never came within the 150 m rider-presence radius (her qualifying fix count is 0, mean distance about 519 m) and that she sent no locating or coordinating message, so POL-NS-04 does not apply. But POL-NS-06 is drafted as strict liability on the waiting period: the rider's absence does not convert a 240-second hold into a compliant 300-second one, and the accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable because the trace shows a single in-geofence interval and the only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09103-01) is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. No driver compensation is payable on a shortfall — POL-NS-06 gives none — and his anti-farming position under POL-NS-07 is not reached, because compensation only arises where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not. As he correctly noted, his lifetime prior_no_show_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and is not the trailing-30-day counter POL-NS-07 reads.\n\nThe record is clean: no clock skew, no trace gap, the chat log is complete against the recorded message count, and the fare reconciles, so no artifact is impaired and no escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 applies. The charge is refunded in full."
